<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Each sentence describes the locus of a moving point. Choose the construction that gives it.</p><ol><li><p>A surveyor stands at points where the ends A and B of a straight wall are seen at an angle of <m>30^\circ</m>.</p><div>[ the perpendicular bisector of AB | a circle with centre A | a pair of lines parallel to l | the bisectors of the angles between the lines | arcs of circles through A and B ]  </div></li><li><p>A sprinkler is moved so that it stays the same distance from two straight hedges that meet at a corner.</p><div>[ the perpendicular bisector of AB | a circle with centre A | a pair of lines parallel to l | the bisectors of the angles between the lines | arcs of circles through A and B ]  </div></li><li><p>A tractor drives so that it is always 3 m from the straight fence l, on either side.</p><div>[ the perpendicular bisector of AB | a circle with centre A | a pair of lines parallel to l | the bisectors of the angles between the lines | arcs of circles through A and B ]  </div></li><li><p>A boda boda rider goes round a roundabout, always 12 m from its centre A.</p><div>[ the perpendicular bisector of AB | a circle with centre A | a pair of lines parallel to l | the bisectors of the angles between the lines | arcs of circles through A and B ]  </div></li></ol></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Ask two questions about each rule: is it about a distance or an angle, and is the distance measured from a point or from a line?</p><ul><li><p>The same distance from two points A and B: the perpendicular bisector of AB.</p></li><li><p>A fixed distance from one point A: a circle with centre A.</p></li><li><p>A fixed distance from a straight line l: a pair of lines parallel to l, one on each side.</p></li><li><p>The same distance from two straight lines that meet: the bisectors of the angles between them.</p></li><li><p>A fixed angle at which AB is seen: arcs of circles through A and B.</p></li></ul><p>Sentence 1: A surveyor stands at points where the ends A and B of a straight wall are seen at an angle of <m>30^\circ</m>. This is arcs of circles through A and B.</p><p>Sentence 2: A sprinkler is moved so that it stays the same distance from two straight hedges that meet at a corner. This is the bisectors of the angles between the lines.</p><p>Sentence 3: A tractor drives so that it is always 3 m from the straight fence l, on either side. This is a pair of lines parallel to l.</p><p>Sentence 4: A boda boda rider goes round a roundabout, always 12 m from its centre A. This is a circle with centre A.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>arcs of circles through A and B</p></answer>
    <answer><p>the bisectors of the angles between the lines</p></answer>
    <answer><p>a pair of lines parallel to l</p></answer>
    <answer><p>a circle with centre A</p></answer>
</stack-static>